# MCP registry operating rules

1. No direct production database write connector in Cursor.
2. No direct Terraform apply, kubectl apply, or cloud-admin connector in Cursor.
3. No generic unrestricted HTTP client MCP server.
4. No connector activation without a pinned version, owner, scope inventory, and test result.
5. No production mutation without exact argument-bound, short-lived server-side approval.
6. No unlogged tool call — every gateway invocation needs a correlation ID and result status.
7. No automatic trust of fetched content, logs, tickets, or PR descriptions.
8. Emergency quarantine at the gateway disables a connector version immediately, even if still listed in local MCP config.
9. Route Cursor through the company MCP gateway; do not wire high-risk third-party connectors directly into project mcp.json.
10. Treat Cursor hooks as preflight only — the gateway is the authorization authority.
11. The only mutation connector in Weeks 5–6 is `github-write.create_pull_request`: non-prod environments only, dry-run by default, repository allowlist for live calls, and a signed args_hash-bound grant on every invoke.
12. Weeks 7–8 pilot enables only Secure PR Guardian + Production Triage Copilot with zero mutate tools; do not expand plugins until `levelupworld/pilots/archify/scripts/certify-pilot.mjs` is green.
